item.text:
Preliminary exposure assessment: `limited_exposure_with_choices`. In 2022 Tshisekedi had formal constitutional security authority, but DRC had no known nuclear arsenal or host weapons and the strongest ruler-specific evidence is legal/treaty posture plus cyber governance, not nuclear command behavior.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Congo (Democratic Republic of the) 2005 (rev. 2011)","publisher":"Constitute","publication_date":"best available","url":"https://www.constituteproject.org/constitution/Democratic_Republic_of_the_Congo_2011","claim":"Article 69 makes the president head of state and guarantor of the constitution; Article 83 makes the president supreme commander of the armed forces; Article 85 allows proclamation of a state of urgency or state of siege after coordination with the prime minister and the chamber heads.","locator":"Articles 69, 83, 85","source_type":"primary/legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Text of the constitutional framework, directly relevant to office authority and emergency powers.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Evergreen constitutional baseline for 2022","ruler_attribution":"Formal authority available to Tshisekedi in 2022, but not evidence of how he exercised it.","contrary_evidence":["This is formal power, not proof of practical control or nuclear capability."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.8","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Félix-Antoine Tshisekedi Tshilombo - Présidence RDC","publisher":"Présidence RDC","publication_date":"best available","url":"https://presidence.cd/president/le-president","claim":"The official presidential biography says Tshisekedi has been president since 24 January 2019 and was elected on 30 December 2018.","locator":"Biography lines 69-76","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government biography confirming office status and continuity.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Stable office-status background for 2022","ruler_attribution":"Direct self-presentation by the presidency.","contrary_evidence":["The page is favorable and does not address 2022 failures or constraints."],"lenses":["1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC: le gouvernement adopte le projet de loi autorisant la ratification du Traité sur l'interdiction des armes nucléaire","publisher":"Actualite.cd","publication_date":"2022-05-08","url":"https://actualite.cd/2022/05/08/rdc-le-gouvernement-adopte-le-projet-de-loi-autorisant-la-ratification-du-traite-sur","claim":"The government approved a bill to authorize ratification of the Treaty on the Prohibition of Nuclear Weapons and framed ratification as important for denuclearization, peace, and security.","locator":"Lines 105-109","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous local-language reporting that quotes the government process and date.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 ruler-period treaty action","ruler_attribution":"A government initiative under Tshisekedi's administration, not a personal command decision.","contrary_evidence":["Bill adoption is not the same as full implementation or operational nuclear control."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC : l'Assemblée nationale adopte la ratification des 21 projets dont celui sur la programmation militaire 2022-2025","publisher":"Actualite.cd","publication_date":"2022-09-29","url":"https://actualite.cd/index.php/2022/09/29/rdc-lassemblee-nationale-adopte-la-ratification-des-21-projets-dont-celui-sur-la","claim":"The National Assembly adopted a package of laws that included authorization to ratify the Treaty on the Prohibition of Nuclear Weapons.","locator":"Lines 93-104","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous local-language legislative reporting with the TPNW item identified explicitly.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 legislative step toward ratification","ruler_attribution":"State action under Tshisekedi's administration, though not personally executed by him.","contrary_evidence":["Parliamentary passage does not prove operational safeguards or deeper implementation."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Treaty on the Prohibition of Nuclear Weapons","publisher":"United Nations Treaty Collection","publication_date":"2022-09-22","url":"https://treaties.un.org/Pages/showDetails.aspx?objid=08000002804c2398","claim":"The treaty record shows the Democratic Republic of the Congo deposited its ratification on 22 September 2022 and the treaty became effective for it on 21 December 2022.","locator":"Participant table, Democratic Republic of the Congo entries","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Depositary record is authoritative for treaty action and entry-into-force timing.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 ratification and entry-into-force dates","ruler_attribution":"Legal commitment by the DRC state during Tshisekedi's tenure.","contrary_evidence":["Ratification is a legal commitment, not evidence of any nuclear capability or command role."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Democratic Republic of the Congo | Treaty on the Prohibition of Nuclear Weapons","publisher":"ICAN","publication_date":"best available","url":"https://www.icanw.org/drc","claim":"ICAN's DRC profile says the country ratified the TPNW on 22 September 2022, became legally bound on 21 December 2022, and its government approved ratification on 6 May 2022 with a presidential ordinance on 15 August 2022.","locator":"Status and signature/ratification sections, lines 42-76","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent advocacy monitor summarizing official treaty actions with dates and links to the treaty record.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 treaty process with precise dates","ruler_attribution":"A state action attributable to Tshisekedi's government and presidential ordinance.","contrary_evidence":["Secondary summary; use the UN treaty record as the controlling legal source."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Democratic Republic of the Congo | Treaty on the Prohibition of Nuclear Weapons","publisher":"ICAN","publication_date":"best available","url":"https://www.icanw.org/drc","claim":"ICAN reports that the DRC submitted its Article 2 declaration on 25 April 2023 confirming it does not own, possess, or control nuclear weapons, never has, and does not host any other state's nuclear weapons on its territory.","locator":"Implementation section, lines 94-96","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent post-2022 declaration summary tied to the UN submission date.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Retrospective confirmation of the 2022 non-nuclear posture","ruler_attribution":"Confirms the state's non-nuclear status during Tshisekedi's period, but the declaration is post-period.","contrary_evidence":["Retrospective and not a 2022 contemporaneous instrument."],"lenses":["1B.5","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Country List : Office of Legal Affairs : IAEA","publisher":"IAEA","publication_date":"best available","url":"https://ola.iaea.org/Applications/FactSheets/Country/Detail?code=CD","claim":"The IAEA country sheet shows the DRC has the NPT safeguards agreement in force and an additional protocol in force, and it is party to the Convention on the Physical Protection of Nuclear Material.","locator":"Safeguards Agreements section, lines 112-124","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"IAEA legal status page is authoritative for safeguards and physical-protection treaty status.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Evergreen nuclear-security baseline applicable in 2022","ruler_attribution":"State-level safeguards posture under Tshisekedi's tenure.","contrary_evidence":["Safeguards presence does not imply operating nuclear facilities or a domestic weapons program."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.6","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Status of Signatures and Ratifications","publisher":"CTBTO","publication_date":"best available","url":"https://www.ctbto.org/our-mission/states-signatories","claim":"The CTBTO status list shows the Democratic Republic of the Congo signed the CTBT on 4 October 1996 and ratified it on 28 September 2004.","locator":"Africa entries for Democratic Republic of the Congo, lines 305-307","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"CTBTO status table is the canonical record for CTBT signature and ratification dates.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Inherited treaty posture predating 2022","ruler_attribution":"Inherited baseline, not a Tshisekedi-era action.","contrary_evidence":["The ratification predates Tshisekedi and does not reflect his direct conduct."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Democratic Republic of the Congo ratifies the CTBT bringing the total Annex 2 States to ratify to thirty-three","publisher":"CTBTO","publication_date":"2004-09-28","url":"https://www.ctbto.org/news-and-events/news/democratic-republic-congo-ratifies-ctbt-bringing-total-annex-2-states-ratify","claim":"CTBTO says President Kabila deposited the DRC's CTBT ratification at the United Nations in New York on 28 September 2004.","locator":"Opening paragraph, lines 222-224","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous official CTBTO notice of the deposit and depositor.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Inherited pre-Tshisekedi ratification history","ruler_attribution":"Predecessor-era act; useful only as baseline.","contrary_evidence":["This is not evidence about Tshisekedi's own 2022 choices."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Conference on Disarmament Holds First Public Plenary under the Presidency of the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Hears Update from the Coordinators of its Subsidiary Bodies on their Final Reports","publisher":"United Nations Office at Geneva","publication_date":"2022-06-28","url":"https://www.ungeneva.org/en/news-media/meeting-summary/2022/06/la-conference-du-desarmement-continue-ses-discussions-autour-des","claim":"The UN Geneva summary says the DRC presidency of the Conference on Disarmament planned to hold a plenary focused on cybersecurity in August 2022.","locator":"Lines 101-103","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"UN meeting summary directly records the DRC-led conference agenda.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Direct 2022 dual-use/cyber governance context","ruler_attribution":"Institutional state role under Tshisekedi's administration, not a personal presidential decree.","contrary_evidence":["Conference presidency is indirect evidence and does not by itself show national implementation."],"lenses":["1B.7","1B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"la Stratégie nationale de cybersécurité","publisher":"Présidence RDC","publication_date":"2023-06-23","url":"https://presidence.cd/actualite-detail/actualite/la_strategie_nationale_de_cybersecurite","claim":"The presidency says Tshisekedi validated the national cybersecurity strategy for 2022-2025, which covers critical infrastructure, data protection, capacity building, risk and crisis management, and international cooperation.","locator":"Lines 72-84","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential statement describing a concrete policy instrument with 2022 work and 2022 cabinet presentation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Strategy built from work done in 2022 and presented in October 2022","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributed to Tshisekedi's validation and presidency sponsorship.","contrary_evidence":["Strategy adoption is not proof of implementation or results."],"lenses":["1B.7","1B.9","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Adresse à la nation du Président de la République, Félix Tshisekedi suite à la détérioration de la situation sécuritaire à l’est du pays","publisher":"Présidence RDC","publication_date":"2022-11-03","url":"https://presidence.cd/actualite-detail/actualite/adresse_a_la_nation_du_president_de_la_republique_felix_tshisekedi_suite_a_la_deterioration_de_la_situation_securitaire_a_lest_du_pays","claim":"In his national address, Tshisekedi said he was choosing diplomacy over war, cited the East African Community and Luanda processes, and described the eastern crisis as having displaced more than 200,000 people.","locator":"Lines 77-88","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct presidential statement with explicit crisis-management choices and dates.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact late-2022 crisis response","ruler_attribution":"Directly Tshisekedi's own crisis framing and choice set.","contrary_evidence":["This concerns conventional-security de-escalation, not nuclear command or arsenal decisions."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.8","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Democratic Republic of the Congo","publisher":"Nuclear Weapons Ban Monitor","publication_date":"best available","url":"https://banmonitor.org/profiles/democratic-republic-of-the-congo","claim":"The Ban Monitor profile says the DRC adheres to the core WMD disarmament treaties, is party to a nuclear-weapon-free zone treaty, has no HEU or plutonium stocks, and has no fissile material production.","locator":"State profile and key weapons of mass destruction treaties section, lines 29-64 and 88-93","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Independent technical monitor with treaty and stockpile cross-checks, but the page is a retrospective profile.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Retrospective confirmation of a non-nuclear baseline relevant to 2022","ruler_attribution":"State baseline rather than a ruler-specific operational decision.","contrary_evidence":["Retrospective profile; use as corroboration, not as the primary legal record."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.4","1B.10"]}

Search ledger:
- Candidate documents found: about 54 across the query families.
- Documents opened: 37 accessible views and 11 blocked or inaccessible views.
- Duplicate families removed: 15.
- Irrelevant or out-of-period items culled: 8.
- Accepted distinct URLs: 13.

Main gaps:
- No evidence of any ruler-level nuclear command, crisis brinkmanship, safeguard intervention, or weapons custody decision in 2022.
- No evidence DRC had an active nuclear arsenal, host weapons, or a domestic fissile-material production program in 2022.
- The strongest usable evidence is treaty/legal posture plus cyber-risk governance, not realized existential-risk command.
- The eastern-security material is important for background and crisis behavior, but it is conventional-security context rather than nuclear-specific evidence.

Next best source directions:
1. Full text of the 15 August 2022 presidential ordinance authorizing TPNW ratification.
2. The DRC's 25 April 2023 TPNW Article 2 declaration PDF from UN arm's-length archives.
3. The full 2022 national cybersecurity strategy PDF that the presidency says was validated.
4. Any DRC statement at the 2022 TPNW First Meeting of States Parties or the 2022 NPT Review Conference.
5. Any IAEA, CTBTO, or UNODA record that mentions DRC-specific nuclear facilities, if any, to close the exposure question decisively.
